The valley is covered in mist, twilight has already fallen. You and your friends Doyle, Conan, and Irene are making your way closer and closer to the edge of the island through the coastal shrubbery. Black, crooked branches often appear from the fog. They sway like being alive. It's cool outside, chilly wind is blowing. Frequently one can hear grinding sounds. Such sound is made by ice floes during the floating of ice, when their edges clash...
Finally the shrubbery is passed and you come to the edge of the island. Usually it looks like an edge of a chasm but today everything is different. Today behind the edge of your house unknown and mysterious lands are floating by. This is the very Wild Island where Cyrus Paganel was on the expedition. How often you heard about it, and now see with your own eyes.
"Quickly!" screams Conan. "Or we won't make it!"
Your friends run towards the edge and jump over one by one. There is Doyle already on the other side waving you with his hand.
"Henry! Come to us."
You rush to meet them. There is the edge of the island, there is the scaring chasm. The Wild Island is slowly floating ahead, and the chasm alike black river. 